{"name":"Flickery C64","hex":"#4f81ff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flickery","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Seeming to flicker; unsteady"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flickery"}],"entries":[{"title":"Commodore 64","blocks":[{"text":"The Commodore 64, also known as the C64, is an 8-bit home computer introduced in January 1982 by Commodore International. It has been listed in the Guinness World Records as the best-selling desktop computer model of all time, with independent estimates placing the number sold between 12.5 and 17 million units. Volume production started in early 1982, marketing in August for US$595. Preceded by the VIC-20 and Commodore PET, the C64 took its name from its 64 kibibytes (65,536 bytes) of RAM. With support for multicolor sprites and a custom chip for waveform generation, the C64 could create superior visuals and audio compared to systems without such custom hardware."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Commodore-64-Computer-FL.jpg/330px-Commodore-64-Computer-FL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commodore_64","wikidata":"Q99775"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/C64_startup_animiert.gif/330px-C64_startup_animiert.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/C64_startup_animiert.gif/330px-C64_startup_animiert.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Commodore 64 startup screen","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AC64_startup_animiert.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/CBM64Cartridges.JPG/500px-CBM64Cartridges.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb